%% Negative SRSW fixture.  glp.tex Remark "Guards and SRSW": "if the success of
%% a guard implies that X? is bound to a ground term, then both X and X? may
%% occur multiple times in the clause."  A negated guard ~g succeeds where g
%% fails (GLP-Spec appendix-guards), so the success of ~ground(X?) implies that
%% X? is NOT ground, and "a negated guard narrows nothing" (TGLP typed-glp.tex,
%% "Type checking of guards").  It licenses no multiple occurrence, and X?
%% occurring twice in the body under it is an SRSW violation.  Until 2026-09-27
%% the analyzer marked the argument of a negated guard grounded exactly as the
%% positive guard's, and this loaded.  Its positive counterpart, under ground/1
%% itself, is srsw/ground_guard_multi_ok.glp's integer/1.
procedure k(_?, _).
k(X, Y?) :- ~ground(X?) | pair(X?, X?, Y).

procedure pair(_?, _?, _).
pair(_, _, done).
